---
description: Require verified facts and explicit handling of unknowns throughout EQCAMP work
alwaysApply: true
---

# No guessing

- Never invent requirements, repository state, command results, package behavior, credentials, or test outcomes.
- Resolve unknowns in this order: inspect the repository and environment, consult the accepted specification and ADRs, check current official documentation, then run a focused experiment or test.
- Clearly distinguish verified facts from inferences. Record any necessary low-risk implementation inference in the relevant decision log.
- If an unresolved choice could change data integrity, security, the domain model, cost, deployment, or destructive behavior, stop only that workstream and ask the user.
- For reversible low-risk details not fixed by the specification, choose the simplest option consistent with existing decisions only after verifying the tools and APIs involved.
- Never claim a command or test passed unless its actual result was observed.
- Do not silently substitute a different requirement when a requested capability cannot be implemented.

